hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20534","Abu 'Ubaydah 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil narrated to us, Salm, meaning Ibn Zurayr, and Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafah, that his grandfather 'Arfajah ibn As'ad had his nose cut off in the Jahiliyyah on the day of al-Kulab, so he took a nose of silver, but it rotted on him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him to take a nose, meaning of gold."
"20535","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafah narrated to us, from his grandfather 'Arfajah ibn As'ad, that his nose was cut off on the day of al-Kulab in the Jahiliyyah, then he mentioned the hadith the like of it."
"20536","'Abdullah narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab al-'Utaridi Ja'far ibn Hayyan narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafah ibn 'Arfajah narrated to us, he said: And 'Abd al-Rahman claimed that he saw 'Arfajah, he said: 'Arfajah's nose was cut off on the day of al-Kulab, so he took a nose of silver, but it rotted on him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him to take a nose of gold."
"20537","Abu 'Amir al-'Adawi Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab informed me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafah ibn 'Arfajah ibn As'ad, that his grandfather 'Arfajah ibn As'ad had his nose cut off in the Jahiliyyah on the day of al-Kulab, then he mentioned the hadith. Abu al-Ashhab said: And 'Abd al-Rahman claimed that he had seen his grandfather, meaning 'Arfajah."
"20538","Muhammad ibn Tamim al-Nahshali narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafah ibn 'Arfajah ibn As'ad, from his grandfather 'Arfajah ibn As'ad, that his nose was cut off on the day of al-Kulab in the Jahiliyyah, then he mentioned the like of it."
"20539","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Hayyan, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafah ibn 'Arfajah narrated to me, that his grandfather 'Arfajah had his nose cut off on the day of al-Kilab, then he mentioned the hadith."
"20540","Yahya ibn 'Uthman, meaning al-Jarmi the broker, narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Hayyan al-'Utaridi, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Tarafah ibn 'Arfajah, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: His nose was cut off on the day of al-Kulab, meaning a water source over which they fought in the Jahiliyyah, then he mentioned the like of it. He said: But it did not rot on me."
"20541","'Abdullah narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman al-Kufi, he said: I saw al-Mughirah ibn 'Abdullah having bound his teeth with gold, and the like of that was mentioned to Ibrahim, and he said: There is no harm in it."
"20542","'Abdullah Abu 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: Some people of hadith came and sought permission to see Abu al-Ashhab, and he gave them permission, and they said: Narrate to us. He said: Ask. They said: We have nothing with us to ask you about. So his daughter said from behind the curtain: Ask him about the hadith of 'Arfajah ibn As'ad whose nose was cut off on the day of al-Kulab."
"20543","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn 'Ilaqah, he said: I heard 'Arfajah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There will be troubles and troubles, so whoever wants to split the affair of this ummah while they are united, strike him with the sword, whoever he may be."
"20544","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: A man from Banu Salit narrated to me that he passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was sitting at the door of the mosque, wearing a Qitri garment with nothing else on him, wrapped in it, while he was saying: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him nor forsake him. Piety is here. And he pointed with his hand to his chest."
"20545","Isma'il narrated to us, from Yunus, Abu al-'Ala' ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated to me, one of Banu Sulaym narrated to me, and I do not think but that he had seen the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, tests His servant by what He gives him; whoever is content with what Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, apportions to him, Allah blesses it for him and widens it; and whoever is not content, He does not bless it for him."
